  "benchmark": "A frozen learned policy plays at least 100,000 fresh 200bb HUNL Slumbot hands, scores above 0 bb/100, and has a 95% confidence-interval lower bound above 0.",
  "hypothesis": "With fresh on-policy data, MGDA residual updates will retain common-descent geometry and produce a nonnegative 4k-to-8k matched learning slope across two seeds while preserving Standard10, both seats, and cross-anchor breadth.",
  "material_change": "Train ordinary control and MGDA treatment on their own fresh on-policy trajectories for two seeds, 8,192 hands per arm per seed (32,768 actual environment hands). Persist Adam across two 4,096-hand chunks, save frozen checkpoints at 4k and 8k, and evaluate all checkpoints on preregistered common untouched decks: 512 mirrored pairs per three anchors per seed. Fixed Standard10 base, +/-0.25 residual cap, 32 stratified update steps per chunk.",
  "baseline": "Two offline cohorts reproduced MGDA common descent on 64/64 steps. Combined 24,576-hand matched evaluation was pooled +3.907 bb/100 CI[-5.580,13.393], with all anchor and seat point estimates positive; one cohort passed all breadth gates and one was mixed.",
  "source": "Frozen Standard10 plus three fixed learned anchors; new on-policy physical-v6 hands.",
